      "schema:url": "https://www.st.nmfs.noaa.gov/plankton/time-series/ru-10101/",
      "schema:description": "White Sea Hydrology and Zooplankton Time Series: Kartesh D1. The ongoing monitoring program have been accomplished since 1957, on a regular basis - since 1961. Sampling is conducted once 10 days in warm period (ice-free) and in March-April and once a month from December through February. Station depth is 60-65 m depending on tide phase and positioning accuracy. Standard horizons are sampled by vertical hauls: 10-0 m, 25-10 m and bottom-25 m. Standard Juday net with opening diameter 37 cm and 200-µm mesh size is used. ",
